    "Correct for severe downward bias: The model consistently overestimates prices by 5-10 EUR when the market is in a downtrend (prices falling from ~79 to ~67), failing to capture the magnitude of the drop.",
    "Adjust for extreme lag in mean reversion: The model predicts a slow, linear recovery, whereas the true market exhibits a sharp V-shaped rebound (spiking from ~67 to ~80) approximately 15-20 days into the forecast horizon.",
    "Incorporate sentiment-triggered volatility: Positive sentiment spikes (value 1.00) in the history often precede sharp price drops or rapid recoveries that the model's smooth trajectory misses; increase forecast volatility when sentiment history contains consecutive high values.",
    "Reduce forecast horizon optimism: The model's long-term forecast (days 20-30) assumes a steady climb, but actual outcomes show high volatility and a return to lower levels (~72-76) after the spike; flatten the tail of the forecast curve.",
    "Apply a 'crash correction' heuristic: If recent history shows a decline from >78 to <75, immediately lower the forecast by at least 3-4 EUR to account for the momentum of the drop, rather than relying on the model's mean-reversion logic."
